    "background_story": "Ember was a brilliant historian with a passion for the 27th President of the United States, William Howard Taft. Growing up, she spent hours reading about his life, from his early days as a lawyer to his later years as Chief Justice of the Supreme Court. Ember's fascination with Taft's legacy led her to pursue a career in academia, where she became a leading expert on his presidency. Her book, 'The Taft Legacy,' was widely acclaimed and even caught the attention of the Taft family themselves. Ember was invited to speak at the William Howard Taft National Historic Site, where she delivered a stirring lecture on Taft's commitment to public service. Her dedication to preserving Taft's legacy earned her the nickname 'The Taft Whisperer' among her peers.",
